1
00:00:01,789 --> 00:00:02,919
(Episode 79)

2
00:00:02,989 --> 00:00:05,959
The driver of the car, a Mr. Han, died at the scene,

3
00:00:06,229 --> 00:00:07,359
and a passenger, a boy with the surname Han,

4
00:00:07,429 --> 00:00:08,429
was injured.

5
00:00:08,489 --> 00:00:09,959
He was taken to the emergency room at Saejuk Hospital...

6
00:00:10,029 --> 00:00:11,029
and is receiving treatment.

7
00:00:11,559 --> 00:00:13,399
The police believe the accident was caused...

8
00:00:13,469 --> 00:00:15,329
by the car behind them attempting to pass...

9
00:00:15,569 --> 00:00:17,799
and are investigating the exact circumstances...

10
00:00:17,869 --> 00:00:19,269
based on witness statements.

11
00:00:20,369 --> 00:00:22,009
A car-plunge accident?

12
00:00:23,209 --> 00:00:25,309
Team Leader Ko, didn't you say your birth name was Han Gyeol?

13
00:00:25,649 --> 00:00:27,779
The injured person here is also a boy with the surname Han,

14
00:00:27,849 --> 00:00:30,119
- and he's seven years old. - I think that's me.

15
00:00:30,449 --> 00:00:33,019
And the local police station was Jeongbin Police Station.

16
00:00:34,319 --> 00:00:39,659
But this article says the car fell,

17
00:00:40,089 --> 00:00:42,329
so in the scene from your dream, by any chance...

18
00:00:42,729 --> 00:00:43,759
No.

19
00:00:44,659 --> 00:00:47,829
Just my father's face, covered in blood...

20
00:00:49,599 --> 00:00:53,169
But if the car fell in the crash, how did I survive?

21
00:00:54,609 --> 00:00:57,679
Could someone have pulled me out before it fell?

22
00:00:58,109 --> 00:01:01,449
This article might not be about your accident, Team Leader Ko,

23
00:01:02,349 --> 00:01:06,689
but the date of the accident, May 16, matches your birthday,

24
00:01:07,019 --> 00:01:08,889
and the accident also happened in Jeongbin.

25
00:01:10,859 --> 00:01:12,889
My father's name is Han Su Cheol.

26
00:01:13,229 --> 00:01:15,059
He was 37 at the time of the accident,

27
00:01:15,699 --> 00:01:17,099
and the last name and age match.

28
00:01:25,709 --> 00:01:26,709
Seo Gwon Sik.

29
00:01:27,839 --> 00:01:28,839
What's wrong with you?

30
00:01:31,609 --> 00:01:33,749
I mean, what are you, some kind of mole?

31
00:01:34,749 --> 00:01:36,479
Just because you're done looking for your mother's daughter,

32
00:01:36,949 --> 00:01:38,319
you're digging into my past?

33
00:01:39,689 --> 00:01:41,119
What makes you so high and mighty?

34
00:01:43,289 --> 00:01:44,359
Coming from a murderer.

35
00:01:48,459 --> 00:01:49,459
What?

36
00:01:50,029 --> 00:01:51,099
Am I wrong?

37
00:01:52,329 --> 00:01:53,429
You know I'm right.

38
00:01:54,069 --> 00:01:55,639
Han Su Cheol's murderer.

39
00:01:58,499 --> 00:02:01,109
- I can't believe them. - Yes.

40
00:02:01,939 --> 00:02:04,409
I shouldn't have gone to you 25 years ago.

41
00:02:04,679 --> 00:02:06,649
If only I hadn't gone to see you then...

42
00:02:09,219 --> 00:02:10,549
Twenty-five years ago?

43
00:02:13,789 --> 00:02:15,419
(Managing Director's Office)

44
00:02:15,589 --> 00:02:16,589
What? Money?

45
00:02:17,089 --> 00:02:18,289
Did you just say money?

46
00:02:23,599 --> 00:02:25,569
Dae Chi. Ko Dae Chi.

47
00:02:27,129 --> 00:02:28,229
Wait a minute...

48
00:02:28,599 --> 00:02:31,069
Sung Jun and Gwon Sik?

49
00:02:33,769 --> 00:02:34,769
That's right.

50
00:02:35,439 --> 00:02:38,979
They had completely lost touch after high school graduation,

51
00:02:39,509 --> 00:02:41,849
and that was the first time the three of us met.

52
00:02:43,849 --> 00:02:44,879
Let go of me, you bastard.

53
00:02:48,919 --> 00:02:52,289
You begged and pleaded for me to save your life,

54
00:02:52,789 --> 00:02:53,859
and now this?

55
00:02:54,829 --> 00:02:56,499
You regret coming to me that day?

56
00:02:57,999 --> 00:03:00,469
If it weren't for me back then, you'd be a dead man.

57
00:03:00,729 --> 00:03:02,469
You and your family, if it weren't for me...

58
00:03:02,539 --> 00:03:04,499
- Don't you dare mention my family. - Why?

59
00:03:04,769 --> 00:03:07,739
Is it because you don't want your family to know what you did?

60
00:03:09,109 --> 00:03:10,239
I see.

61
00:03:10,909 --> 00:03:12,309
Because they can't find out...

62
00:03:12,379 --> 00:03:14,849
their trusted father and husband is a murderer.

63
00:03:14,909 --> 00:03:16,049
Shut up, you son of a gun.

64
00:03:20,119 --> 00:03:21,249
You bastard.

65
00:03:25,829 --> 00:03:28,789
What do you all think you're doing?

66
00:03:28,929 --> 00:03:30,929
Men who are nearly 60, acting like this.

67
00:03:31,829 --> 00:03:33,099
What will you do...

68
00:03:33,169 --> 00:03:36,199
if the Chairman sees you in this state?

69
00:03:36,339 --> 00:03:37,339
What will you do?

70
00:03:41,109 --> 00:03:43,439
Honestly, these people.

71
00:03:44,039 --> 00:03:45,749
What? What's going on?

72
00:03:49,419 --> 00:03:50,419
What are you doing here?

73
00:03:50,879 --> 00:03:52,749
It's nothing.

74
00:03:53,949 --> 00:03:54,989
Gyeol.

75
00:03:55,659 --> 00:03:58,219
You took vacation time, but you're back at work already?

76
00:03:58,589 --> 00:04:00,129
I should go home.

77
00:04:00,729 --> 00:04:01,929
Instead of this,

78
00:04:01,989 --> 00:04:03,999
how about we go out for some team bonding...

79
00:04:04,059 --> 00:04:05,499
for the first time in a while?

80
00:04:05,929 --> 00:04:07,829
A team get-together? What is the occasion?

81
00:04:07,899 --> 00:04:09,899
Do we really need a reason for a team get-together?

82
00:04:10,599 --> 00:04:12,439
It can be an after-party for the living funeral,

83
00:04:12,909 --> 00:04:14,339
and we can celebrate you two becoming...

84
00:04:14,409 --> 00:04:15,979
the official Gangsu Construction couple.

85
00:04:16,109 --> 00:04:19,809
And to get us fired up for the competition's third round.

86
00:04:19,879 --> 00:04:22,079
For all those reasons. What do you think, Jo Eun Ae?

87
00:04:22,249 --> 00:04:24,649
I am fine with it. What about you, Manager Seo?

88
00:04:24,779 --> 00:04:25,919
I am fine with it, too.

89
00:04:25,989 --> 00:04:28,289
Well, in that case, I will have to go with the majority.

90
00:04:41,699 --> 00:04:42,969
Twenty-five years ago.

91
00:04:44,469 --> 00:04:46,239
If only you all had not shown up...

92
00:04:49,079 --> 00:04:50,409
This is driving me crazy.

93
00:04:50,479 --> 00:04:51,979
(Gangsu Construction)

94
00:04:56,949 --> 00:04:59,189
Jo Sung Jun, Seo Gwon Sik.

95
00:05:00,449 --> 00:05:02,719
What are you two doing here?

96
00:05:14,029 --> 00:05:15,169
You disloyal bastards.

97
00:05:16,799 --> 00:05:19,369
You cut off all contact right after high school,

98
00:05:19,739 --> 00:05:21,669
and now you show up after over ten years,

99
00:05:21,739 --> 00:05:23,509
and the first thing you say to me is...

100
00:05:24,879 --> 00:05:25,879
money?

101
00:05:27,909 --> 00:05:29,749
Do I look like an ATM to you?

102
00:05:33,649 --> 00:05:35,819
I know it is not my place to interfere,

103
00:05:37,159 --> 00:05:39,689
but Dae Chi, please help him out just this once.

104
00:05:41,259 --> 00:05:43,829
Gwon Sik did not want to come, but I dragged him here.

105
00:05:44,729 --> 00:05:48,369
Right now, who else but you can help save Gwon Sik?

106
00:05:49,139 --> 00:05:51,069
Anyone else but you, man,

107
00:05:52,139 --> 00:05:55,069
should not have done that to me. Do you understand?

108
00:05:56,579 --> 00:05:57,879
Dae Chi, I am begging you.

109
00:05:58,309 --> 00:06:00,709
If he cannot avoid bankruptcy this time, the guy is finished.

110
00:06:02,049 --> 00:06:03,549
Are you Gwon Sik's spokesman?

111
00:06:03,619 --> 00:06:05,749
Why do you keep talking when he should be?

112
00:06:21,169 --> 00:06:22,229
Hey, Seo Gwon Sik.

113
00:06:22,939 --> 00:06:24,199
What do you think you are doing?

114
00:06:24,999 --> 00:06:27,939
Come on. Gwon Sik, get up. Get up and talk.

115
00:06:29,479 --> 00:06:30,809
Please, just help me this once.

116
00:06:33,179 --> 00:06:34,409
Save me, Dae Chi.

117
00:06:36,249 --> 00:06:37,949
My youngest child is not even one yet.

118
00:06:39,119 --> 00:06:40,789
My oldest just started kindergarten.

119
00:06:42,889 --> 00:06:44,159
If I go down like this...

120
00:06:46,329 --> 00:06:47,429
My family...

121
00:06:50,799 --> 00:06:51,899
Oh, man...

122
00:07:02,439 --> 00:07:04,779
Oh, what brings you here?

123
00:07:05,809 --> 00:07:08,349
Why are you drinking all alone in the dark?

124
00:07:10,049 --> 00:07:12,689
Strong liquor on an empty stomach will upset your stomach.

125
00:07:15,349 --> 00:07:17,019
I do not know what happened,

126
00:07:17,919 --> 00:07:19,019
but work things out.

127
00:07:20,159 --> 00:07:23,699
I will bring you the first-aid kit, so put on some ointment and sleep.

128
00:07:24,699 --> 00:07:26,599
Mother...

129
00:07:28,529 --> 00:07:29,639
Please don't tell Father...

130
00:07:30,169 --> 00:07:31,569
Of course.

131
00:07:32,299 --> 00:07:35,739
When have I ever told him anything about your affairs?

132
00:07:36,339 --> 00:07:37,609
Do not worry.

133
00:07:39,079 --> 00:07:40,079
Thank you.

134
00:07:54,159 --> 00:07:55,999
What happened to your face?

135
00:07:56,659 --> 00:07:57,929
Did you get into a fight?

136
00:07:58,959 --> 00:08:00,429
What fight?

137
00:08:02,169 --> 00:08:03,339
Look at me.

138
00:08:04,799 --> 00:08:07,409
You did. You got into a fistfight.

139
00:08:08,269 --> 00:08:10,939
Don't tell me. Was it with President Ko?

140
00:08:11,579 --> 00:08:13,509
It is nothing. Do not worry.

141
00:08:13,909 --> 00:08:15,979
It is always nothing.

142
00:08:16,779 --> 00:08:18,179
What is going on between you two that...

143
00:08:18,249 --> 00:08:19,649
you are still getting into fistfights?

144
00:08:20,189 --> 00:08:23,059
Are you two still hot-blooded high schoolers?

145
00:08:23,759 --> 00:08:26,389
Why are you two so desperate to destroy each other?

146
00:08:26,789 --> 00:08:30,099
- The kids will hear. Stop it. - The kids are not here.

147
00:08:30,699 --> 00:08:31,759
So tell me.

148
00:08:32,229 --> 00:08:34,199
Even at the Chairman's living funeral,

149
00:08:34,469 --> 00:08:36,539
I had a feeling something was going on between you.

150
00:08:36,699 --> 00:08:38,269
What is it?

151
00:08:38,699 --> 00:08:39,869
It is just...

152
00:08:40,309 --> 00:08:41,939
When we were looking for Madam's daughter,

153
00:08:42,709 --> 00:08:44,879
he had a grudge because I hid it from him,

154
00:08:45,709 --> 00:08:47,949
and we argued about it and things got physical.

155
00:08:48,809 --> 00:08:49,819
Satisfied now?

156
00:08:53,189 --> 00:08:54,489
This is unbelievable.

157
00:08:55,449 --> 00:08:56,559
Honestly.

158
00:09:00,859 --> 00:09:03,829
Writer Jo, when our webtoon first launches,

159
00:09:04,059 --> 00:09:05,499
how do you think it will do?

160
00:09:07,069 --> 00:09:08,769
We will just have to wait and see.

161
00:09:09,469 --> 00:09:10,839
Well, obviously.

162
00:09:12,139 --> 00:09:17,079
I am cautiously predicting around 30,000 views initially.

163
00:09:17,209 --> 00:09:18,809
What? To get numbers like that,

164
00:09:18,879 --> 00:09:21,249
you have to build a loyal readership,

165
00:09:21,549 --> 00:09:24,379
- and that takes at least a month. - No.

166
00:09:24,849 --> 00:09:26,019
I bet my prediction will be right.

167
00:09:27,019 --> 00:09:28,489
Do you want to make a bet?

168
00:09:28,549 --> 00:09:30,959
Maybe the winner gets a wish granted or...

169
00:09:31,019 --> 00:09:33,589
What makes you so confident?

170
00:09:34,029 --> 00:09:36,599
For starters, the original "The ER Witch"...

171
00:09:36,659 --> 00:09:38,659
is already a massive bestseller,

172
00:09:38,729 --> 00:09:41,769
and now it is being combined with my unique art style.

173
00:09:41,829 --> 00:09:45,339
It is absolutely guaranteed to be a huge hit.

174
00:09:51,709 --> 00:09:54,679
Why? Are you going to be Cinderella and run off at 11 o'clock?

175
00:09:54,979 --> 00:09:56,219
Cinderella? Please.

176
00:09:56,679 --> 00:09:58,279
We have not even finished this instalment.

177
00:10:03,459 --> 00:10:06,029
Aren't you a little hungry?

178
00:10:06,359 --> 00:10:08,959
The packed lunches we brought today were kind of small.

179
00:10:09,399 --> 00:10:10,399
What?

180
00:10:14,669 --> 00:10:16,899
Yes, well, I guess so.

181
00:10:17,639 --> 00:10:19,939
Then how about we go get some ramyeon?

182
00:10:22,169 --> 00:10:23,279
We can eat ramyeon...

183
00:10:23,779 --> 00:10:24,809
and then go?

184
00:10:25,439 --> 00:10:26,479
What did you just say?

185
00:10:27,079 --> 00:10:29,079
Why would I "eat ramyeon and then go" with you?

186
00:10:30,749 --> 00:10:31,919
Who said anything about that?

187
00:10:31,979 --> 00:10:33,749
I meant eat ramyeon and then come back to work.

188
00:10:34,619 --> 00:10:36,119
Let's just go to the convenience store...

189
00:10:36,189 --> 00:10:37,189
for some cup ramyeon.

190
00:10:38,059 --> 00:10:39,259
Well, if you don't want to, I'll just go alone.

191
00:10:43,799 --> 00:10:44,959
Convenience store ramyeon?

192
00:10:46,199 --> 00:10:49,769
Jo Eun Nim, what were you thinking? Is your mind in the gutter?

193
00:10:50,169 --> 00:10:51,839
Gosh.

194
00:10:54,869 --> 00:10:57,109
Writer Jo, do not be like that. Let's go together.

195
00:10:57,379 --> 00:10:58,909
You must be hungry too.

196
00:10:59,709 --> 00:11:01,409
Should I? All right, then.

197
00:11:07,119 --> 00:11:09,389
Any news on what you were looking into?

198
00:11:10,019 --> 00:11:12,989
Nothing is set in stone yet. I need to observe a little longer.

199
00:11:13,929 --> 00:11:16,729
But are we not supposed to be here for team bonding?

200
00:11:17,259 --> 00:11:19,359
- Let's talk about something else. - Okay, let's.

201
00:11:20,969 --> 00:11:23,599
How are things, Jo Eun Ae? Is Gyeol treating you well?

202
00:11:23,939 --> 00:11:26,839
Sorry? Yes, of course he is.

203
00:11:28,309 --> 00:11:31,579
I thought he would never date anyone his entire life.

204
00:11:31,639 --> 00:11:34,679
Goodness. Jo Eun Ae, I was so surprised...

205
00:11:34,749 --> 00:11:37,019
when I saw the cake on Gyeol's birthday.

206
00:11:37,249 --> 00:11:40,219
I knew it right then. Game over.

207
00:11:41,289 --> 00:11:42,719
Jo Eun Ae, you are truly amazing.

208
00:11:43,619 --> 00:11:44,919
It was nothing.

209
00:11:45,489 --> 00:11:46,529
You are amazing.

210
00:11:46,859 --> 00:11:50,799
You opened a door that Min Ho and I could never open.

211
00:11:51,399 --> 00:11:54,529
But do you know Gyeol plans to return to the US...

212
00:11:54,599 --> 00:11:55,829
after this competition?

213
00:11:57,039 --> 00:12:00,169
- Yes, I know. - So what are your plans?

214
00:12:00,439 --> 00:12:03,979
Are you going with him? Or try a long-distance relationship?

215
00:12:04,709 --> 00:12:08,209
- That is a bit too long-distance. - That has not happened yet.

216
00:12:08,779 --> 00:12:10,879
No one knows what tomorrow will bring.

217
00:12:16,689 --> 00:12:17,859
But Gyeol,

218
00:12:18,419 --> 00:12:19,829
was your original surname Han?

219
00:12:24,259 --> 00:12:25,299
Yes.

220
00:12:26,059 --> 00:12:27,099
Han Gyeol.

221
00:12:27,999 --> 00:12:30,799
- That's my real name. - That's right, Han Gyeol.

222
00:12:31,299 --> 00:12:33,109
It has been a long time since I have heard that name.

223
00:12:33,809 --> 00:12:36,109
That is why his personality is so consistent.

224
00:12:46,549 --> 00:12:51,059
All right, to wish us luck in the third competition,

225
00:12:51,389 --> 00:12:53,989
shall we all make a toast? All right, raise your glasses.

226
00:12:54,629 --> 00:12:56,899
When I say "Fair," you say "Play." Okay?

227
00:12:57,429 --> 00:12:58,959
- Okay, fair. - Play.

228
00:12:59,029 --> 00:13:00,599
- Play. - Play.

229
00:13:05,499 --> 00:13:08,369
That must have been tough. I wanted to go with you today,

230
00:13:08,439 --> 00:13:10,439
but I thought it wouldn't be right if I also took the day off.

231
00:13:10,579 --> 00:13:11,779
Of course. You did the right thing.

232
00:13:12,139 --> 00:13:14,409
I'll focus more on the competition from now on.

233
00:13:14,749 --> 00:13:17,049
- By the way... - Do you want to go in first?

234
00:13:17,119 --> 00:13:18,949
I'm going to check on Cho Rong for a bit.

235
00:13:19,349 --> 00:13:20,919
I feel like I've been neglecting her lately,

236
00:13:20,989 --> 00:13:25,089
- with work and everything. - Okay. Tell Cho Rong I'm sorry...

237
00:13:25,159 --> 00:13:26,489
for taking up all of your time.

238
00:13:26,929 --> 00:13:29,129
- Okay. - Wait a minute.

239
00:13:29,359 --> 00:13:30,359
Yes?

240
00:13:30,429 --> 00:13:32,399
(Grandma Pancake)

241
00:13:33,999 --> 00:13:36,129
My goodness. Really?

242
00:13:36,569 --> 00:13:38,939
- Don't be too late. - Okay.

243
00:13:40,939 --> 00:13:42,509
Oh, honestly.

244
00:13:46,249 --> 00:13:49,378
- What are you doing here? - Hey. What a surprise.

245
00:13:49,379 --> 00:13:50,419
You've been so busy with your new romance...

246
00:13:50,479 --> 00:13:52,019
I thought you'd forgotten all about me.

247
00:13:52,919 --> 00:13:55,489
I'm sorry. What's with the flowers?

248
00:13:56,459 --> 00:13:57,859
I got them as a gift.

249
00:13:58,219 --> 00:13:59,629
A gift? From who?

250
00:14:00,229 --> 00:14:01,229
It's a secret.

251
00:14:01,289 --> 00:14:04,059
Eun Ae, there's something I want to ask you.

252
00:14:04,629 --> 00:14:07,399
- This isn't about me. - A friend of a friend?

253
00:14:07,499 --> 00:14:08,829
How did you know?

254
00:14:08,899 --> 00:14:10,869
That's what people always say when they want advice.

255
00:14:10,939 --> 00:14:11,939
"This isn't about me."

256
00:14:12,239 --> 00:14:14,639
But this really isn't about me.

257
00:14:17,409 --> 00:14:21,549
So, you're saying a guy she never, ever saw romantically,

258
00:14:21,609 --> 00:14:24,579
she's suddenly developing feelings for him?

259
00:14:24,649 --> 00:14:26,289
That's what she said.

260
00:14:27,089 --> 00:14:29,419
Whenever she thinks about him, her pulse starts to race,

261
00:14:29,489 --> 00:14:31,519
and her heart pounds at random times.

262
00:14:31,989 --> 00:14:35,989
- Isn't that arrhythmia? - Come on. Arrhythmia? Seriously?

263
00:14:36,089 --> 00:14:39,399
Ham Cho Rong, you know me, right? You know how clueless I am.

264
00:14:39,599 --> 00:14:41,269
Of course I know that.

265
00:14:41,329 --> 00:14:43,499
If you're asking someone like me for relationship advice,

266
00:14:43,969 --> 00:14:45,469
do you really think I can give you a proper answer?

267
00:14:45,539 --> 00:14:46,539
Well, that's true.

268
00:14:46,609 --> 00:14:49,169
But you seem to be doing well with Team Leader Ko.

269
00:14:49,309 --> 00:14:51,409
I thought you were totally innocent, but you're making a lot of progress.

270
00:14:51,639 --> 00:14:55,249
We shared 2 kisses and 2 pecks.

271
00:14:55,549 --> 00:14:57,749
No, three. That's it.

272
00:14:58,519 --> 00:14:59,519
What was that?

273
00:14:59,579 --> 00:15:01,289
Don't tell me Grandma is awake and listening to us.

274
00:15:01,989 --> 00:15:04,389
Don't worry about that. I checked her room earlier,

275
00:15:04,459 --> 00:15:06,629
and she was fast asleep.

276
00:15:07,559 --> 00:15:08,559
By the way,

277
00:15:08,629 --> 00:15:09,629
how's Team Leader Ko doing these days?

278
00:15:09,829 --> 00:15:10,929
Is he having fewer nightmares?

279
00:15:11,529 --> 00:15:13,629
I think he is, a little.

280
00:15:14,199 --> 00:15:16,539
The problem is that they're not dreams,

281
00:15:16,599 --> 00:15:17,599
they're memories.

282
00:15:18,239 --> 00:15:19,239
And one day,

283
00:15:19,299 --> 00:15:20,809
those memories will come back completely.

284
00:15:21,339 --> 00:15:25,309
To be honest, I'm scared he'll have an even harder time then.

285
00:15:25,879 --> 00:15:27,549
Memories? What are you talking about?

286
00:15:27,809 --> 00:15:31,049
I'll tell you when I can.

287
00:15:31,319 --> 00:15:32,649
Okay, I get it.

288
00:15:38,959 --> 00:15:40,859
What are you doing out here? Why didn't you go in?

289
00:15:41,089 --> 00:15:42,789
I was waiting for you. There's something I have to say.

290
00:15:43,759 --> 00:15:44,859
Can you sit for a moment?

291
00:15:48,769 --> 00:15:49,969
What is it?

292
00:15:51,269 --> 00:15:53,539
Your mother has given up...

293
00:15:53,609 --> 00:15:56,639
being legally registered as your grandmother’s daughter.

294
00:15:56,979 --> 00:15:58,639
What? What do you mean?

295
00:16:01,379 --> 00:16:05,219
She knows we can't break up, so she wants us to date openly.

296
00:16:05,549 --> 00:16:07,549
I think your mother made a sacrifice for us.

297
00:16:08,519 --> 00:16:09,649
That's unbelievable.

298
00:16:10,389 --> 00:16:12,959
I never even thought about that issue.

299
00:16:13,589 --> 00:16:14,729
Neither did I.

300
00:16:15,159 --> 00:16:17,199
But on the day of the living funeral,

301
00:16:17,259 --> 00:16:19,259
after facing my parents' disapproval,

302
00:16:19,829 --> 00:16:22,229
I think that's when your mother made up her mind.

303
00:16:23,099 --> 00:16:26,839
Oh no. It was so hard for Mom and Grandma to reunite.

304
00:16:28,169 --> 00:16:30,639
They only just found each other after 50 years,

305
00:16:30,709 --> 00:16:33,039
and it seems like we've made them half a family.

306
00:16:33,849 --> 00:16:35,149
I feel awful about it too.

307
00:16:35,449 --> 00:16:37,019
My heart aches.

308
00:16:37,719 --> 00:16:41,689
I'm sure Mom wanted to be officially listed as her mother's daughter.

309
00:16:42,649 --> 00:16:46,019
My mom is always like this. Her children come before her,

310
00:16:46,119 --> 00:16:47,589
and her family is everything.

311
00:16:48,159 --> 00:16:52,059
- That means we have to do better. - Yes.

312
00:16:52,329 --> 00:16:54,799
She made that decision because she was afraid...

313
00:16:54,869 --> 00:16:56,799
we'd get hurt by what people think,

314
00:16:57,239 --> 00:16:59,369
so we absolutely can't show any sign of wavering.

315
00:16:59,569 --> 00:17:01,469
Good. Then that's settled.

316
00:17:02,009 --> 00:17:06,179
Oh, and tomorrow, let's clock out right at six o'clock.

317
00:17:06,409 --> 00:17:08,109
What? Why clock out on time all of a sudden?

318
00:17:08,409 --> 00:17:11,549
There's something I want to do now.

319
00:17:11,979 --> 00:17:13,349
Let's do it tomorrow.

320
00:17:16,459 --> 00:17:18,319
Yes, I'm about to go to sleep.

321
00:17:20,589 --> 00:17:21,959
You sleep well too, General Director.

322
00:17:22,889 --> 00:17:23,899
Okay.

323
00:17:46,489 --> 00:17:47,789
Hey. You just smiled.

324
00:17:49,349 --> 00:17:52,059
You know that's the first time you've smiled all day?

325
00:17:53,689 --> 00:17:54,689
Anyway,

326
00:17:55,129 --> 00:17:59,029
that was the day Ko Min Ho became Seo Seung Ri's willing captive.

327
00:17:59,869 --> 00:18:04,239
And just like that, 5 years, then 10, just flew by.

328
00:18:05,169 --> 00:18:07,039
But you never changed your mind,

329
00:18:07,839 --> 00:18:10,179
and neither have my feelings for you.

330
00:18:13,179 --> 00:18:16,179
You'd think you'd give up by now.

331
00:18:17,979 --> 00:18:21,519
You know better than anyone words like that don't work, right?

332
00:18:24,619 --> 00:18:25,619
Right.

333
00:18:27,229 --> 00:18:28,459
Here, a present.

334
00:18:29,259 --> 00:18:31,058
What is this?

335
00:18:31,059 --> 00:18:34,199
I saw it at the convenience store while getting ramyeon, so I got it.

336
00:18:34,869 --> 00:18:36,269
I didn't just find this by chance, you know?

337
00:18:36,999 --> 00:18:40,109
Give me your arm. There.

338
00:18:50,079 --> 00:18:51,719
What is it? Is there something you want to say?

339
00:18:55,549 --> 00:18:57,059
No matter how much I think about it,

340
00:18:57,459 --> 00:19:00,589
I think something is seriously wrong with your dad.

341
00:19:00,959 --> 00:19:02,929
Why? Did something else happen?

342
00:19:04,099 --> 00:19:05,659
At the Chairman's living funeral,

343
00:19:05,729 --> 00:19:08,029
your dad looked like he was having a hard time.

344
00:19:08,569 --> 00:19:10,239
At the Chairman's event,

345
00:19:10,669 --> 00:19:13,199
especially after seeing the Chairman almost collapse,

346
00:19:13,509 --> 00:19:14,939
is he the kind of person to just go home?

347
00:19:16,469 --> 00:19:19,779
I think he must have gotten some kind of huge shock that day.

348
00:19:20,309 --> 00:19:21,379
A shock?

349
00:19:22,179 --> 00:19:24,019
When we were all dancing and having fun,

350
00:19:24,079 --> 00:19:25,219
I vaguely saw something.

351
00:19:25,949 --> 00:19:29,449
I think Gyeol was on a call near your dad.

352
00:19:30,289 --> 00:19:32,159
The look on your dad's face when he saw that...

353
00:19:33,529 --> 00:19:34,589
It was like...

354
00:19:35,189 --> 00:19:38,629
the face of someone who had received a terrible shock.

355
00:19:39,329 --> 00:19:43,229
What do you mean? Why would Dad care if Gyeol was on a call?

356
00:19:43,439 --> 00:19:44,439
I know.

357
00:19:45,039 --> 00:19:48,009
I know it makes no sense, but...

358
00:19:53,079 --> 00:19:55,549
What was that call about? You looked upset.

359
00:19:56,049 --> 00:19:58,049
It was from the police station. We'll talk later.

360
00:19:58,179 --> 00:19:59,479
Okay, I get it.

361
00:20:02,049 --> 00:20:04,919
Actually, while I was cleaning your dad's study earlier,

362
00:20:05,489 --> 00:20:07,829
I saw a strange note.

363
00:20:08,629 --> 00:20:12,699
It mentioned something about a car accident in 2001.

364
00:20:13,259 --> 00:20:15,299
A car accident in 2001?

365
00:20:16,899 --> 00:20:17,999
Anyway...

366
00:20:18,769 --> 00:20:21,339
I think something is going on,

367
00:20:21,909 --> 00:20:23,539
but I don't know what it is.

368
00:20:25,139 --> 00:20:28,849
Why am I keeping my tired daughter up like this?

369
00:20:29,379 --> 00:20:30,719
Okay, go get some rest.

370
00:20:31,619 --> 00:20:32,619
Okay.

371
00:20:35,789 --> 00:20:37,259
The year 2001...

372
00:20:38,059 --> 00:20:39,059
Could it be?

373
00:20:43,729 --> 00:20:46,669
No. What am I thinking?

374
00:21:00,409 --> 00:21:03,309
Where did he go so early in the morning?

375
00:21:05,049 --> 00:21:06,079
No, that can't be it.

376
00:21:06,479 --> 00:21:08,689
I don't remember him coming into the room last night.

377
00:21:10,389 --> 00:21:11,389
Oh my.

378
00:21:13,729 --> 00:21:14,889
Hello, good morning.

379
00:21:15,329 --> 00:21:16,489
- Min Ho. - Yes?

380
00:21:16,559 --> 00:21:17,559
Have you seen your father?

381
00:21:17,929 --> 00:21:20,329
Father? Isn't he in his room?

382
00:21:20,399 --> 00:21:22,899
No, he's not in his room or the study.

383
00:21:23,739 --> 00:21:26,199
What on earth is going on with him?

384
00:21:26,739 --> 00:21:28,439
Don't tell me he stayed out all night.

385
00:21:29,069 --> 00:21:30,279
What are you talking about?

386
00:21:31,079 --> 00:21:33,779
- He stayed out all night? - Good morning, Grandfather.

387
00:21:33,909 --> 00:21:36,209
Yes. No, that's not it.

388
00:21:36,349 --> 00:21:38,349
I just don't remember him coming to our room last night,

389
00:21:38,419 --> 00:21:40,349
and he's gone now that I'm up.

390
00:21:40,449 --> 00:21:41,449
I was just wondering if...

391
00:21:41,519 --> 00:21:44,889
No, that's not it. I saw him come in yesterday.

392
00:21:44,959 --> 00:21:46,089
What are you talking about?

393
00:21:46,519 --> 00:21:48,059
You saw him? Really?

394
00:21:48,159 --> 00:21:51,659
He left for work early. He said he had a breakfast meeting.

395
00:21:51,729 --> 00:21:54,729
- What? At dawn? - Come in.

396
00:21:55,129 --> 00:21:58,439
- Breakfast is ready. - Okay, got it.

397
00:21:59,399 --> 00:22:00,809
Mom, you should get changed and come out too.

398
00:22:01,009 --> 00:22:03,639
- Okay, you go on ahead. - Okay.

399
00:22:05,279 --> 00:22:07,609
Did you really see him?

400
00:22:07,909 --> 00:22:11,749
- Min Ho's dad coming in? - Would I lie? What for?

401
00:22:11,949 --> 00:22:13,619
President Ko came in, and Chief Seo left.

402
00:22:13,819 --> 00:22:16,149
I saw it clearly with my own two eyes.

403
00:22:16,349 --> 00:22:17,759
Stop making wild assumptions...

404
00:22:17,819 --> 00:22:19,889
and accusing an innocent man. Good grief.

405
00:22:20,019 --> 00:22:23,029
My goodness. Who am I accusing? Why is he being like that?

406
00:22:24,159 --> 00:22:25,329
- Dad. - Yes?

407
00:22:25,399 --> 00:22:29,229
From now on, are you going to take me to and from kindergarten?

408
00:22:29,299 --> 00:22:31,399
Yes, until my special summer classes start.

409
00:22:31,839 --> 00:22:33,909
But Grandma has to pick you up today.

410
00:22:34,109 --> 00:22:35,669
I have an appointment before my class.

411
00:22:36,109 --> 00:22:37,239
Okay, Dad.

412
00:22:37,979 --> 00:22:40,879
Thank you for the meal. I'll go get ready for kindergarten.

413
00:22:40,949 --> 00:22:42,208
- Okay, go ahead. - Go ahead.

414
00:22:42,209 --> 00:22:43,949
So, what's your appointment today?

415
00:22:44,619 --> 00:22:47,489
Ji Seon called and asked to meet.

416
00:22:47,989 --> 00:22:48,989
Ji Seon did?

417
00:22:49,889 --> 00:22:50,889
Do you know what it's about?

418
00:22:51,519 --> 00:22:53,489
Our cooling-off period is almost over.

419
00:22:54,259 --> 00:22:55,889
We have to make a final decision.

420
00:22:56,589 --> 00:22:58,259
Has it been that long already?

421
00:22:59,259 --> 00:23:03,269
Eun Hyung, I'm begging you. Don't let Ji Seon go, okay?

422
00:23:03,399 --> 00:23:05,369
It's Ji Seon's choice to make.

423
00:23:06,439 --> 00:23:09,409
I'm just going to respect her decision.

424
00:23:09,469 --> 00:23:11,779
Think carefully and make the best choice.

425
00:23:12,209 --> 00:23:14,649
Don't forget that Bit Na is your top priority.

426
00:23:15,549 --> 00:23:18,319
- Yes, Father. Thanks for the meal. - Okay.

427
00:23:19,119 --> 00:23:21,019
- Have a good day, Eun Hyung. - Thanks.

428
00:23:21,089 --> 00:23:22,989
I'm sorry. I overslept a little.

429
00:23:23,449 --> 00:23:25,419
Well, you came in late last night too.

430
00:23:25,689 --> 00:23:27,029
Haven't you been working too much lately?

431
00:23:27,259 --> 00:23:30,299
No, sir. We all went out for drinks with the General Director yesterday.

432
00:23:30,399 --> 00:23:31,829
You were drinking yesterday?

433
00:23:31,899 --> 00:23:34,469
If I'd known, I would've made some hangover soup.

434
00:23:34,669 --> 00:23:37,769
It's all right. I didn't drink much. Thank you for the food.

435
00:23:37,839 --> 00:23:38,839
All right, then.

436
00:23:39,199 --> 00:23:41,569
Mom, why did you do that?

437
00:23:42,439 --> 00:23:44,479
- Do what? - I heard you.

438
00:23:45,009 --> 00:23:46,078
Why would you give up...

439
00:23:46,079 --> 00:23:47,809
being on Grandma’s family register because of us?

440
00:23:47,909 --> 00:23:52,319
Goodness, you'll be late for work. Stop with the nonsense and just eat.

441
00:23:55,589 --> 00:23:57,359
Is Eun Nim still sleeping?

442
00:23:57,419 --> 00:23:59,589
Eun Nim? I didn't see her in her room.

443
00:23:59,989 --> 00:24:03,159
What? Eun Nim didn't come home yesterday?

444
00:24:04,129 --> 00:24:06,929
- That brat! I swear... - What's wrong now?

445
00:24:06,999 --> 00:24:10,499
She probably worked all night and fell asleep in her studio.

446
00:24:10,569 --> 00:24:11,569
No, absolutely not.

447
00:24:11,639 --> 00:24:13,469
Everyone, just finish eating and go to work.

448
00:24:13,539 --> 00:24:14,539
What? Gosh...

449
00:24:15,109 --> 00:24:16,109
I mean...

450
00:24:17,239 --> 00:24:18,309
What's with your mom?

451
00:24:18,739 --> 00:24:19,979
I know, right?

452
00:24:24,079 --> 00:24:25,279
Jo Eun Nim, open the door.

453
00:24:26,779 --> 00:24:27,789
Aren't you going to open it?

454
00:24:28,419 --> 00:24:29,419
Jo Eun Nim!

455
00:24:34,489 --> 00:24:37,329
- What do we do? What time is it? - What? It's...

456
00:24:38,099 --> 00:24:39,829
It's nine.

457
00:24:40,199 --> 00:24:42,369
Nine? But my curfew hasn't started yet.

458
00:24:42,429 --> 00:24:45,839
No, no, that's not it. It's nine in the morning. Morning.

459
00:24:45,899 --> 00:24:49,639
What? Oh, what should I do? Did we stay here all night again?

460
00:24:50,139 --> 00:24:51,139
Aren't you going to open the door?

461
00:24:51,409 --> 00:24:54,379
I know you're both in there. Open this door right now.

462
00:24:54,749 --> 00:24:55,749
What do we do?

463
00:24:55,809 --> 00:24:58,549
I think we're doomed today.

464
00:24:58,849 --> 00:25:01,518
Shouldn't we hold a living funeral for ourselves today?

465
00:25:01,519 --> 00:25:02,889
Just a moment.

466
00:25:03,449 --> 00:25:04,459
Oh, seriously.

467
00:25:05,189 --> 00:25:06,189
Oh, my.

468
00:25:07,459 --> 00:25:10,559
Mom, we were working and meant to take a short break,

469
00:25:10,629 --> 00:25:12,829
but I guess we fell asleep at the desk. I'm sorry.

470
00:25:13,429 --> 00:25:16,269
I'm sorry. If only I hadn't suggested we eat ramyeon.

471
00:25:16,329 --> 00:25:18,539
Sorry?

472
00:25:18,669 --> 00:25:21,609
What is with you, Mom? Nothing happened between us.

473
00:25:21,739 --> 00:25:24,339
We were working and just fell asleep at the desk. That's all.

474
00:25:24,439 --> 00:25:27,179
- Is that really all? - What? Yes, of course.

475
00:25:27,249 --> 00:25:28,649
I only looked at...

476
00:25:28,709 --> 00:25:29,949
Eun Nim's sleeping face and then...

477
00:25:30,009 --> 00:25:32,819
What? You only looked at her face?

478
00:25:32,979 --> 00:25:34,789
Yes, and I gently...

479
00:25:34,849 --> 00:25:36,449
held her hand like this...

480
00:25:36,519 --> 00:25:38,319
Her hand too? What else?

481
00:25:38,389 --> 00:25:39,759
And then, on her cheek...

482
00:25:39,819 --> 00:25:41,529
like this...

483
00:25:41,589 --> 00:25:43,129
- Bung Woo! - You scared me!

484
00:25:43,189 --> 00:25:44,498
What did you just say?

485
00:25:44,499 --> 00:25:48,599
- You jerk. You punk. - Why do you keep hitting him?

486
00:25:48,929 --> 00:25:50,969
Right, I shouldn't be blaming someone else's kid.

487
00:25:51,039 --> 00:25:53,939
- You deserve this. - Oh, no, you can't do that.

488
00:25:54,009 --> 00:25:55,709
Just hit me instead. Please?

489
00:25:55,769 --> 00:25:59,039
- Unbelievable. You two. - Mom, stop it.

490
00:26:02,779 --> 00:26:04,519
Please stop hitting him. Stop.

491
00:26:06,549 --> 00:26:08,289
If you hit him one more time...

492
00:26:08,849 --> 00:26:10,089
If I hit him, what?

493
00:26:10,149 --> 00:26:12,959
You said there was nothing between you two.

494
00:26:13,019 --> 00:26:15,129
You said you were just collaborators.

495
00:26:15,359 --> 00:26:17,899
I like Bung Woo.

496
00:26:18,899 --> 00:26:19,899
What?

497
00:26:20,899 --> 00:26:23,629
- What did you say? - Because he's the man I like.

498
00:26:24,199 --> 00:26:26,369
So, please just stop it.

499
00:26:26,799 --> 00:26:28,939
Bung Nim.

500
00:26:32,409 --> 00:26:34,749
(Gangsu Construction)

501
00:27:24,229 --> 00:27:27,229
(Seoul District Court Ruling)

502
00:27:27,429 --> 00:27:29,299
With the front of the defendant's vehicle...

503
00:27:30,129 --> 00:27:31,139
Han Su Cheol...

504
00:27:32,569 --> 00:27:35,009
Struck the side of the victim's vehicle...

505
00:27:35,069 --> 00:27:36,369
on the driver's side.

506
00:27:41,149 --> 00:27:42,279
Han Su Cheol.

507
00:27:44,619 --> 00:27:45,679
This can't be.

508
00:27:47,089 --> 00:27:48,119
Dad...

509
00:27:49,389 --> 00:27:51,919
Dad did this to Gyeol's father...

510
00:27:58,999 --> 00:27:59,999
Seung Ri.

511
00:28:22,889 --> 00:28:25,819
(Our Happy Days)
